Without Eureka Server
Order → http://localhost:8082

With eureka server
Order → inventory-service

What We Built:

Created discovery-server module

Added @EnableEurekaServer

Added Spring Cloud dependency

Eureka Client Setup (Inventory Service)

eureka.client.service-url.defaultZone=http://localhost:8761/eureka

Eureka Client 
@EnableDiscoveryClient

🔟 Multiple Instances & Load Balancing

We set:

server.port=0

Meaning:

Spring picks random available port.

Then ran service twice → 2 instances registered.

Important fix:

eureka.instance.instance-id=${spring.application.name}:${local.server.port}
1️⃣1️⃣ How Load Balancing Works

When calling:

http://inventory-service/api/inventory

Spring Cloud LoadBalancer:

Fetches all instances from Eureka

Chooses one (round robin)

Forwards request

Interview Answer:

Eureka handles service registry. LoadBalancer handles instance selection.

1️⃣2️⃣ What That “DOWN” Instance Was

Old stale registration

Occurs when instance stops unexpectedly

Removed after lease expiration

Important properties:

eureka.instance.lease-renewal-interval-in-seconds=30
eureka.instance.lease-expiration-duration-in-seconds=90


1️⃣3️⃣ Microservice Communication Flow (Place Order)

Client sends order.

Order service:

Extracts SKU list

Calls inventory service

Inventory service:

DB query using IN clause

Returns list of StockResponse

Order service:

Checks .allMatch(StockResponse::isInStock)

Saves order if true


1️⃣4️⃣ Important Interview Questions
❓ What is Eureka?

Service registry that:

Stores all running service instances.

Allows dynamic service discovery.

❓ Difference between Eureka Client and Server?

Server → Registry

Client → Registers itself & fetches others

❓ What happens if Eureka server goes down?

Services still run.

But new registrations fail.

Service discovery fails.

❓ Why server.port=0?

To allow multiple instances on same machine.

❓ How does load balancing work?

Spring Cloud LoadBalancer:

Fetches instances

Uses round-robin strategy

❓ What is instance-id?

Unique identity of each running service instance.

❓ Why DTO in microservices?

Decoupling

Security

Contract control

❓ What is @Transactional?

Manages DB commit/rollback automatically.


